Ladybird applies math-auto to single-character text. Blink checks
the text length in ApplyMathAutoTransform(), and Gecko checks it in
nsCaseTransformTextRunFactory::TransformString(). WebKit also checks for
a single character in convertToMathAuto(), and has a separate path for
identifiers in RenderMathMLToken::updateMathVariantGlyph().

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all kept sin
upright in an mi element. Chrome and Firefox applied math-auto to a
single x in an HTML span. WebKit left the span upright.
